  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 136 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nHeat remains the main concern through the weekend and into next week \nwith heat indices generally 100-109. A moderate to major risk of \nheat related impacts can be expected across S TX through the period, \nwith an increasing risk to extreme impacts next week across the \nBrush Country. Heat advisory conditions will be possible at times \nduring next week with heat indices of 110-114 across mainly the \nCoastal Bend and Victoria Crossroads where the afternoon humidity \nwill be highest. The mid/upper level high pressure system leading to \nthe increased heat risks will also lead to very low to nil rain \nchances. Models do indicate a couple of weak inverted troughs or \neasterly waves through the period, thus can not rule out an isolated \nshower or two, mainly along the sea breeze.",
